course: dictionary
lesson: 4213
title: One word, many gowns
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives several meanings for gown, so read the words around it to find the right one. Context clues often tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The girl fastened him into the gown, laughing, and said he looked very respectable.» Here a gown is something you put on your body, and the fancy words tell you it is a special dress. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A dress would fit, so gown means a dress.
explain: «He wears a long dressing-gown, carries a flat candlestick, and had probably been on his way to bed.» The bed tells you a dressing-gown is a robe worn at home, not out in the street. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A gown is a long, formal dress, like a ball gown or a wedding gown.
fact: A gown can also be a loose robe worn over clothes for a job or ceremony, such as a judge, a graduate or a surgeon.
fact: A hospital gown is a loose garment that patients wear in hospital.
fact: A dressing gown is a warm robe worn over pyjamas. In the US it is often called a bathrobe.
fact: Doctors and nurses wear gowns to keep germs away, which is an important way to stay clean and healthy.
exercise: «He wears a long dressing-gown, carries a flat candlestick, and had probably been on his way to bed.» What is a dressing-gown? | A swimming costume | A ball dress for a party | *A warm robe worn over pyjamas at home | A judge's black robe in court
exercise: Why do doctors and nurses wear gowns? | To look fancy at a ball | To keep warm in the snow | To hide their faces | *To keep germs away
exercise: «For his money Toad gets a cotton print gown, an apron, a shawl, and a rusty black bonnet.» What is the gown here? | A graduate's cap and gown | *A loose cotton dress worn by a woman | A ball gown with a long train | A dressing gown and slippers
test: At a graduation, what do the students wear? | A swimming costume | A hospital gown | A dressing gown and slippers | *A cap and gown
test: Which kind of gown is worn over pyjamas? | *A dressing gown | A hospital gown | A wedding gown | A ball gown
exam: Mia wore a ball gown that shimmered under the lights at the dance. What kind of gown is it? | A warm robe worn over pyjamas | A judge's robe in court | A loose hospital garment | *A long, formal dress
